-- 5-player WotLK and Cataclysm dungeon spawn masks (5.4.8 mask bits: 2 = normal, 4 = heroic, 6 = both).
-- Zul'Aman and Zul'Gurub spawns were normal only (mask 2), so heroic, the mode the Dungeon Finder uses, was empty.
-- A few WotLK heroic-only spawns (Commander Stoutbeard, Amanitar) were on normal only.
-- Each mask-2 spawn gets the mask of the matching spawn (same entry within 5 yards) in:
--   1. Legends of Azeroth Pandaria 5.4.8 (GPL v2), world DB of 2024-07-22
--   2. TrinityCore TDB 3.3.5 (WotLK; masks 1/2 shifted to 2/4) or TDB 4.4.2 (Cataclysm), GPL v2
-- else the mask LoA gives every spawn of that entry on the map, else (entry LoA never spawns there) the map's full mask.
-- LoA makes ZA and ZG heroic only, as on retail since 4.1, but the core still lets players enter them on normal,
-- so those spawns keep normal as well (mask 6). Spawns LoA disables (mask 0) keep mask 2.
-- The end-of-dungeon chests come in normal/heroic pairs at the same spot: the masks below follow TDB and the loot
-- (heroic chest: item level 200 / 346 loot), so each mode gets only its own chest.
-- Generated by skyfire_port_plan/tools/raidmasks.py (--from 2 --keep 568,859). No database names; safe to run twice.

